# The SQLite mirror is rebuildable from ComCat; keeping it out of git avoids
# committing a ~60 MB binary that changes every run.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash on purpose. Bare "data/" matches ANY directory
# called data at any depth, which silently swallowed web/public/data and would
# have deployed a site with no catalog in it.
/data/

node_modules/
web/dist/
# The emitted catalog IS tracked, all ~1.4 MB of it. It is generated, which
# normally argues for ignoring it -- but committing it means a deploy only has
# to build the front end, instead of re-running a 35-minute backfill. The cost
# is a diff on every refresh.
web/public/data/*.gz

.DS_Store
*.pyc
__pycache__/
